" vi and vim in the box are vim.tiny, which starts in vi-compatible mode: arrow keys and Backspace misbehave
" while typing and nothing shows the mode. These lines make it behave like a current vim.
" To leave: Esc, then :q! and Enter (:wq saves first).
set nocompatible
set backspace=indent,eol,start
set ttimeout ttimeoutlen=50
set showmode showcmd ruler
" The mouse stays with the terminal, so selecting text to copy works inside vim too.
set mouse=
